#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""book-sync -- keep X0urnal++ folder books in step across devices through a git remote.

    book-sync setup  <book>            git init if needed, drivers + filter in .git/config,
                                       .gitattributes, .gitignore, user.name = device (idempotent)
    book-sync init   <book>            setup + first commit + push to the remote (push-to-create)
    book-sync clone  <slug> [<dest>]   clone <remote base>/book-<slug>.git into ~/Documents/notebooks/
    book-sync save   <book>            commit local changes; no network, never touches the files
    book-sync push   <book>            save + send; never touches the files; `behind` if the remote
                                       has changes we do not (then run sync when it is safe)
    book-sync sync   <book>            save, fetch, merge, push (may rewrite page files)
    book-sync status <book>            what the last sync found + what is waiting; no network
    book-sync sync-all                 sync every *.book folder under ~/Documents/notebooks/
    book-sync merge  <book> <ref>      merge a local ref (one2book-sync's `onenote` branch) with
                                       everything sync does around a merge; no network

Every command prints exactly one JSON line on stdout, also when it fails:

    {"state": "synced|offline|conflict|error|local|behind", "time": "2024-01-31T14:02:11",
     "changed": [paths the merge changed in the working tree], "conflicts": [conflict page ids],
     "message": "Merged from laptop", ...extra fields: book, ahead, skipped, busy, books}

Exit status 0 for every state but `error`. The contract is ./README.md; this file's choices
where the README left room are in its "Notes" section.

<book> is a path to a book folder, or the name of one under ~/Documents/notebooks/ ("Notes"
or "Notes.book"). Environment: BOOK_SYNC_REMOTE_BASE (where book repos live, e.g.
git@example.com:me; else `git config book-sync.remote`; no default), BOOK_SYNC_NOTEBOOKS (default
~/Documents/notebooks), BOOK_SYNC_DEVICE (default from the hostname), BOOK_SYNC_LOCK_TIMEOUT
(default 30 s), BOOK_SYNC_GRACE (default 10 s, see reconcile), BOOK_SYNC_STARTED_BY (X0urnal++
on Windows sets it, see open_elsewhere).
"""

